    "created_at": "2016-01-29T07:12:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-29T07:12:41Z",
    "body": "OK, this LGTM as-is, but I have another potential cleanup/consistification. We can continue the discussion in another issue if you want to merge this but now I will put it here.\n\nFor the SVGs that I have introduced, I used `<img>`, since they seemed like images. But for @Hixie's previous two SVGs, he used `<object>` with fallback pngs.\n\nFor content-venn.svg, `<object>` is necessary, since it is interactive. But I noticed that the experience for parsing-model-overview.svg is nicer than for my two `<img>` SVGs, since the text is selectable.\n\nI have three potential suggestions we may want to consider:\n- Use `<object>` for asyncdefer.svg and sample-url.svg, to give the slightly better UX of selectable text and such.\n  - But, what happens to the alt?\n- Get rid of the png fallbacks for content-venn.svg and parsing-model-overview.svg. They seem redundant in this day and age.\n  - But, maybe we still want to support UAs that don't do `<object>`? Like ATs, I assume. Then we would just nest a `<img src=\"....svg\">` inside the `<object data=\"....svg\">`?\n- Finally, we should presumably fix the mismatch between \"setting an alt=\"\" on this would be bogus (indeed, it would be non-conforming and bad for accessibility.)\" and the presence of alt=\"\" on the content-venn.svg fallback `<img>`.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
